1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:02,800
Hi and welcome to The Print.
My name is Karanjeet Kaur.

2
00:00:02,870 --> 00:00:05,400
I'm a writer and an editor.
Let's talk today about Dhurandar.

3
00:00:05,470 --> 00:00:08,700
An early scene in Dhurandar: The Revenge presages
a kind of revisionism present throughout the film.

4
00:00:08,770 --> 00:00:12,600
The intelligence bureau chief, Ajay Sanyal,
played by R. Madhavan,

5
00:00:12,670 --> 00:00:16,800
attempts to enlist a broken Jaskirat Singh Rangi,
a death row convict handpicked from jail.

6
00:00:16,870 --> 00:00:20,500
Jaskirat only wants the release of death,
but Sanyal counters with a rousing Sikh prayer.

7
00:00:20,570 --> 00:00:25,200
Sanyal exhorts: "Sura so pehchaniye jo lade deen ke het,
purja purja kat mare kabhuna chhade khet."

8
00:00:25,270 --> 00:00:29,800
Loosely translated, the lines mean a true spiritual warrior
fights for the rights of the oppressed,

9
00:00:29,870 --> 00:00:34,500
and does not abandon the battlefield
even when his body is demolished part by part.

10
00:00:34,570 --> 00:00:38,200
It's a beautiful, stirring call to courage
deployed by several TV shows and films.

11
00:00:38,270 --> 00:00:42,100
Perhaps its best use is in the 1988
National Award-winning Tamas.

12
00:00:42,170 --> 00:00:46,000
Govind Nihalani's devastating film lies on the opposite
ideological spectrum from Dhurandar.

13
00:00:46,070 --> 00:00:50,500
In Dhurandar: The Revenge, 2016 demonetization
is rebranded Operation Green Leaf.

14
00:00:50,570 --> 00:00:54,800
Pakistani intelligence and underworld operatives,
including a fictionalized Dawood Ibrahim,

15
00:00:54,870 --> 00:00:59,200
funneled ₹60,000 crore in counterfeit notes into India
to buy the Uttar Pradesh elections.

16
00:00:59,270 --> 00:01:03,500
The Prime Minister's televised address from 8th Nov 2016
is lifted wholesale and inserted into the film.

17
00:01:03,570 --> 00:01:07,400
The cost to the economy was estimated at
₹1.28 lakh crore in the first 50 days alone.

18
00:01:07,470 --> 00:01:11,800
Can that figure account for
the scale of human suffering?

19
00:01:11,870 --> 00:01:15,500
The RBI's annual report said 99.3%
of demonetized currency returned to banks.

20
00:01:15,570 --> 00:01:19,400
Black money hoarders survived,
diversifying into real estate in Goa.
